      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THE DEFENDER (4) is the one to beat after putting four wins together, most recently scoring comfortably in CL3 company here despite being held up in the straight. Loves the 1200m and keeps McIver in the saddle. Can continue on his merry way. SUJEED (7) rises out of BM55 grade but gets a major weight drop. Satherley goes back on, and the first-time visors give him scope to sharpen after two sound efforts at this venue. MELO MELO KAVA (6) was solid when third in a CL4 here first-up, has weight relief and should appreciate stretching out the extra 150m this time. DETERMINATION (1) brings proven track-and-trip credentials and gets weight relief after racing wide early when fourth at Mackay. Drawn kinder this time and is one to keep in mind.",
